diff --git a/docs/internationalization.md b/docs/internationalization.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7512a49
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/internationalization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Internationalization
+
+Fizzy speaks English (the default) and Japanese.
+
+## Choosing a language
+
+Open any page with `?locale=ja` (or `?locale=en`) to switch. The choice is kept in the session and, for
+signed-in people, on their `Identity#locale`, so it follows them to new browsers. A choice made before
+signing in is saved to the identity on sign-in. Locales we don't offer are ignored. People who never
+chose anything get English. See `Localization` (`app/controllers/concerns/localization.rb`).
+
+HTTP etags and fragment caches vary by locale (except for the default one, so English keys are unchanged).
+
+## Where strings live
+
+- `config/locales/views/*.{en,ja}.yml`: templates, using lazy lookups (`t(".title")`).
+- `config/locales/helpers`, `models`, `flash`, `shared`: everything outside templates.
+- `config/locales/javascript.*.yml`: strings rendered by Stimulus controllers. They're embedded in each page
+  (`javascript_translations_tag`) and read with `t()` from `helpers/i18n_helpers`.
+- `config/locales/rails.ja.yml`: Rails' own Japanese defaults (dates, numbers, validation messages).
+- `saas/config/locales`: the SaaS engine.
+
+Lazy lookups inside a block yielded from another partial resolve against that partial, so use full keys there.
+
+## Content that isn't rendered per person
+
+- Emails, push notifications, and per-user Turbo Stream broadcasts use the recipient's language
+  (`Identity#with_locale`, `User#with_locale`).
+- Webhooks post to shared destinations, so they always use the default language.
+- System comments are stored in the default language and rebuilt from their event for other languages.
+- The static error pages in `public/` can't know who is looking, so they carry both languages.
+
+## Adding strings
+
+Add every key to both `en` and `ja`. `test/lib/translations_test.rb` fails when they drift apart, and
+missing translations raise in development and test.
